-- title:
--   Node centre, Igusa-side end and layered node rings
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ is assumed, by `hW`, to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is of the places $w$ that are rational, are `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}) \in \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$; one such place $s \in W$ is fixed. The hypothesis `hle` records the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base-changed full modular function field into the function field of the $X_H$-curve of level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`. A `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is given (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with surjective residue map onto the reduced field, kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue field, together with a map on places compatible with degrees and divisors), and `hR₀` demands that $R_0$ compute coefficientwise reduction: a Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral with residue the coefficientwise reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. A natural number `wd` is a free width parameter.
--
--   The base data over a small field consist of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, together with the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ`: the ring $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, it is Henselian, its residue field is algebraically closed, and every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. Further auxiliary data: a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$. A layer family is given: a type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K_n$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ with $A_n = A \cap K_n$, an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0} \le K_n$ for all $n$, and cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in some $K_n$. An element $\pi_t \in A$ with $\pi_t^{q^2-1} = q$ is fixed, and `htame` requires that every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1` fix $K_{n_0}$ pointwise. Finally $K_b$ is the bottom intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ (so `hKb : Kb = ⊥`), $A_b$ the valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, and $\varpi_b \ne 0$ a generator of its maximal ideal.
--
--   With the algebra structure on `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying the four level-field clauses: $F_0$ consists exactly of those $f$ all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$; the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in$ `Gamma0 M'`; and $F_0$ is linearly disjoint from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the sense that for $K'$ finite over $k_0$, elements $a_i$ of the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, and $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   For such an $F_0$, the assertion is further made for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, every subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` with an $A_b$-algebra structure, and every finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$, given: `hjR`, that the image of `jq` in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral; `hjs`, that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; `hJK`, that `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` lies in `fieldBar q M'`; and a Hasse lift $a_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $A$ satisfies `hpin`: its $q$-th power equals the value of $s$ at the $R_0$-residue of $j$.
--
--   The long hypothesis on this datum is a conjunction of the following groups of clauses. (W0-group) $W_0 \cap k_0 = A$, $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and its maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$. (Reading of $s$) For $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral and has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ where $j$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $A$ equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (Equivariance of $W_0$) For $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in$ `Gamma0 M'`, membership in $W_0$ is preserved by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` on elements of $F_0$ whose image also lies in $F_0$. (B-group, summarised here) The structure map $A_b \to B$ is the inclusion $K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`; $B$ is contained in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of that join is a quotient of elements of $B$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $B$ is contained in $W_0$ (its elements lie in $F_0$ and in $W_0$); the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$, and $W_0$ is exactly the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; the image of `jq` lies in $B$, and $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for $\gamma \in$ `Gamma0 M'`; there is an element of $B \cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$, and is residually transcendental at $j$ (no monic $A$-integral polynomial evaluated at $j$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$); for each supersingular place $s' \ne s$ there is an element of $B \cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring of $F_0$ that induces $A$ on $k_0$ and reads values at $s'$ in the sense above; and, for every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ making [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) a domain and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of `rootsOfUnity (q + 1) (GaloisField q 2)` of cardinality `wd` and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) whose kernel is $(\varpi_b)$, which on $A_b$ is reduction to $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$, whose image has the whole quotient field as its field of fractions and equals the image of [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) in [`DrinfeldCurve.drinfeldFunctionField q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L12), and which intertwines `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` with [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) along `redQ q γ` for $\gamma \in$ `Gamma0 M'` with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276). (nodes-group, summarised here) `nodes` has exactly $q+1$ elements; there is a common chart $B_c$, the subring of $F_0$ generated by the image of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, contained in every node, each node being the localisation of $B_c$ at its own units; the nodes are permuted by the `levelAutBar`-operators for $\gamma \in$ `Gamma0 M'`, and for each $\zeta$ any two nodes are matched by some $\gamma \in$ `Gamma0 M'`; distinct nodes are separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; every valuation subring of $F_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$ and reading values at $s$ either contains $B$ or dominates some node. Finally, for each node $O$: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is local and Noetherian; $O \cap k_0 = A$; every element of $O$ is congruent to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ modulo non-units; and there exist an exponent $E_0 \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{wd}}\,v$ for a unit $v$ of $k_0 \cap A$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A \cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, i.e. $\widehat{A\cap k_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$, $\iota$ is the constant map on the image of $k_0 \cap A$, $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$ is a unit there; the Igusa germ clause that `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` $- a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and is carried by $\iota$ to a unit times $V^e$ with $e \ge 1$; the existence of a branch $W_x$, a discrete valuation subring of $F_0$ containing $O$, inducing $A$ on $k_0$, with uniformiser $\pi_0$, carrying an element at which $A$-integral polynomials are residually transcendental, with $c_x$ in its maximal ideal and $c_y$ a unit, whose reading of $R_0$-integral elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` detects vanishing of the $R_0$-residue and, when that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, places the element in $O$ with the expected non-unit difference from constants; this $W_x$ moreover excludes, for each other node, some element of it; and the existence of a chart $B_x \subseteq B \cap O$ whose elements have no poles where $j$ has none, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, $B_x$ providing denominators for all of $F_0$, $B_x$ generated by the image of $k_0 \cap A$ and a finite set, and containing an element lying in no valuation subring of $F_0$ that induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, is residually transcendental at $j$, and fails to contain $O$.
--
--   Under all of this the assertion is: for every field $F_{ss}$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{ss}$ with $R.\mathrm{integers} \cap F_0 = W_0$; for every node $O \in$ `nodes`; for every $E_0 \ge 1$ admitting a unit $v$ of $k_0 \cap A$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{wd}} v$; and for every layer completion datum, namely subrings $C'_l \subseteq A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which are domains and discrete valuation rings with uniformisers $\varpi'_l$, complete discrete valuation rings $W_l$ with uniformisers $\pi_l$, exponents $e_l$ and ring maps $j_l : C'_l \to W_l$, subject to: $C'_l = A \cap K_l$; the residue of $d \in C'_l$ in $A$ vanishes precisely when $\varpi'_l \mid d$; $C'_{n_0} \le C'_l$; $\pi_l$ irreducible; $\pi_0 = v\,(\varpi'_l)^{e_l}$ with $v$ a unit of $C'_l$; $j_l(\varpi'_l) = \pi_l$; $j_l$ reflects divisibility by powers of $\pi_l$; and $j_l$ has dense image ($W_l$ is approximated modulo every power of $\pi_l$) — there exist a place `nd` of $F_{ss}$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$, a field $FI$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$, a `RegularProlongation` $R_x$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $FI$, a place $b_x$ of $FI$, a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$, a set $S$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a subring $\mathcal N$ of `fieldBar q M'`, a family of local Noetherian subrings $\mathcal N_l$ of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $\iota$, and elements $c_x, c_y, c_u$ of `fieldBar q M'`, with the following properties.
--
--   `nd` is rational. $R_x.\mathrm{integers} \cap F_0 = W_x$; $O \subseteq W_x$; $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$. There is an element $c_{yO}$ of $O$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is $c_y$, which is a unit of $W_x$, and which characterises $W_x$ as the smallest such branch: every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and $c_{yO}$ a unit, contains $W_x$. For every other node $O' \ne O$ there is $g \in O \cap O'$ of the form $g = c\,u$ with $c \in O$ mapping to $c_x$ and $u$ a unit of $O$, such that $g$ is a unit of $O'$.
--
--   Next, $O$ is a node; $O$ is contained in $\mathcal N_{n_0}$ and non-units of $O$ stay non-units there; $S$ consists exactly of the places $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ dominating $O$, that is with $O$ inside the valuation subring of $P$ and with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of each non-unit of $O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$; the $R$-residues of elements of $O$ lie in the valuation subring of `nd`, those of non-units of $O$ lie in its maximal ideal, and `nd` is the unique place of $F_{ss}$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ with these two properties. Furthermore $b_x$, `nd` and every $P \in S$ are rational; $\mathcal N$ is exactly $R_x.\mathrm{integers} \cap R.\mathrm{integers}$ intersected with the valuation subrings of all $P \in S$, and $P.\mathrm{evalAt} f \in A$ for $f \in \mathcal N$ and $P \in S$.
--
--   The crossing relation reads $c_x c_y = (\varpi'_{n_0})^{e_{n_0} E_0} c_u$ in `fieldBar q M'`; the $R_x$-residue of $c_x$ is $0$; the order of the $R$-residue of $c_x$ at `nd` is $1$; the $R$-residue of $c_y$ is $0$; the order of the $R_x$-residue of $c_y$ at $b_x$ is $1$. For every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1`, setting $g$ to be the image of $\tau$ under [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M'))`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54), the set $S$ is $g$-stable and $g$ fixes $c_x$ and $c_y$.
--
--   Density: every $f \in$ `fieldBar q M'` is a quotient of two elements of some $\mathcal N_l$ with nonzero denominator, and every $f$ admits a nonzero $b \in \mathcal N_{n_0}$ with $f b$ a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal N_{n_0}$.
--
--   For every $l$: $\mathcal N_{n_0} \le \mathcal N_l \le \mathcal N$; $S$ is also characterised as the set of places dominating $\mathcal N_l$; $C'_l$ maps into $\mathcal N_l$; every element of $\mathcal N_l$ differs from the image of some element of $C'_l$ by a non-unit; elements of $\mathcal N_l$ are linearly independent over $C'_l$ in the same disjointness sense as before; there is a subring $B_x$ of `fieldBar q M'` inside $\mathcal N_l$ containing $c_x$, $c_y$, $c_u$, with $\mathcal N_l$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units and $B_x$ generated by the image of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x, c_y \in \mathcal N_l$ and $c_u$ is a unit of $\mathcal N_l$; and there are a ring map $\sigma : W_l \to$ the adic completion of $\mathcal N_l$ and a ring isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l)` $(\pi_l^{e_l E_0})$ such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$, $\iota_c \circ \sigma$ is the constant embedding, `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` $- a_0$ lies in $\mathcal N_l$ and is carried by $\iota_c$ to a unit times $V^e$ with $e \ge 1$, the images of $C'_l$ lie in the image of $\sigma$, and the two tube readings hold: if $f \in \mathcal N_l$ has nonzero $R_x$-residue of order $n$ at $b_x$, then $\iota_c(f)$ is congruent to a unit times $V^n$ modulo the ideal generated by $\mathrm{const}(\pi_l)$ and $U$; symmetrically, if $f$ has nonzero $R$-residue of order $n$ at `nd`, then $\iota_c(f)$ is congruent to a unit times $U^n$ modulo the ideal generated by $\mathrm{const}(\pi_l)$ and $V$.
--
--   Finally, places in $S$ read the supersingular value: for $P \in S$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-negative order wherever $j$ has, whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that residue, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Moreover $R_0$-integral elements map into $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$, and there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to $FI$ such that the $R_x$-residue of the image of any $R_0$-integral element is $j$ of its $R_0$-residue, and such that membership in the valuation subring of $s$ is equivalent, under $j$, to membership in the valuation subring of $b_x$.
--
--   This is the per-node step in the construction of a semistable model of the full-level modular curve of level $q^2M'$ over a valuation ring above $q$: for one of the $q+1$ node rings of the supersingular fibre attached to a supersingular place $s$, it produces the centre of the node as a rational place of the reduced field, the Igusa-side end of the node together with its branch, the set of places dominating the node, and the layered node rings with their $UV$-crossing presentations $c_xc_y = (\varpi'_{n_0})^{e_{n_0}E_0}c_u$, tube readings of both ends, and inertia invariance. It is the every-prime, free-width form of this step, and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_two_of_dvd) in assembling the node charts over all nodes.
